contradicting messages from Hamas,

415
00:22:05,866 --> 00:22:09,700
so just think about how horrible it is for a family.

416
00:22:09,700 --> 00:22:10,800
"He's alive",

417
00:22:10,800 --> 00:22:11,866
"Now he's dead",  "now he's ...",

418
00:22:12,500 --> 00:22:16,200
it really a vicious

419
00:22:18,166 --> 00:22:19,100
warfare.

420
00:22:25,966 --> 00:22:29,000
Omri Miran, our dear friend,

421
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:35,466
is still held captive in Gaza for over 700 days,

422
00:22:35,666 --> 00:22:37,300
almost two years,

423
00:22:38,833 --> 00:22:42,133
and we hope that he's

424
00:22:42,466 --> 00:22:44,500
as healthy as possible

425
00:22:45,100 --> 00:22:49,900
and we are waiting and praying to get him back.

426
00:22:50,100 --> 00:22:52,166
To get him back.

427
00:22:52,166 --> 00:22:55,233
And to get the body of Joshua Loitu Mollel

428
00:22:55,233 --> 00:22:59,200
back to his family in Tanzania.

429
00:23:01,266 --> 00:23:03,133
Ah, we pray for it.

430
00:23:07,633 --> 00:23:08,600
Anyway...

431
00:23:10,600 --> 00:23:13,366
I was in my house and

432
00:23:13,466 --> 00:23:15,733
my son is handicapped,

433
00:23:15,800 --> 00:23:19,333
back then he used to walk with a walker,

434
00:23:20,633 --> 00:23:25,366
And, the bombardment was so heavy that day, that we all,

435
00:23:25,366 --> 00:23:27,233
were staying in the safe room,

436
00:23:27,233 --> 00:23:30,133
and there was not enough room for the walker,

437
00:23:30,233 --> 00:23:32,300
and besides we thought that...

438
00:23:32,833 --> 00:23:34,266
There were many people,

439
00:23:34,266 --> 00:23:36,900
because we stayed so long

440
00:23:36,900 --> 00:23:38,766
in the safe rooms,

441
00:23:38,766 --> 00:23:42,066
there were many people who used a bucket or a bottle,

442
00:23:42,066 --> 00:23:44,066
if they needed to relieve themselves.

443
00:23:46,100 --> 00:23:47,633
My son couldn’t,

444
00:23:47,633 --> 00:23:50,533
he had to have his accessible toilet.

445
00:23:54,200 --> 00:23:56,333
So, we had to

446
00:23:57,566 --> 00:24:00,866
go out of the safe room a few times that day.

447
00:24:02,066 --> 00:24:04,300
We started thinking about

448
00:24:04,300 --> 00:24:06,466
what would be the safest way to do it,

449
00:24:07,000 --> 00:24:09,166
so we thought that if he goes with the walker,

450
00:24:09,166 --> 00:24:11,100
he will not have enough time to turn around,

451
00:24:11,100 --> 00:24:12,600
if he needs to

452
00:24:12,600 --> 00:24:13,933
come back to shelter.

453
00:24:13,933 --> 00:24:16,300
So we decided we’re going to throw

454
00:24:16,300 --> 00:24:20,033
the walker away for the day and every time he needed

455
00:24:20,033 --> 00:24:21,233
to go,

456
00:24:21,233 --> 00:24:26,633
we just grabbed him, each parent by one shoulder, and

457
00:24:26,633 --> 00:24:32,966
carried him to the toilet. "Operation Toilet",

458
00:24:32,966 --> 00:24:34,400
it was every time now.

459
00:24:34,400 --> 00:24:36,366
Every time like this took a few attempts,

460
00:24:36,366 --> 00:24:38,566
because the bombardment was so heavy.

461
00:24:39,366 --> 00:24:40,700
And there was even one time,

462
00:24:40,700 --> 00:24:41,966
that we already sat him down,

463
00:24:41,966 --> 00:24:44,533
and we had to grab him and run back.

464
00:24:45,366 --> 00:24:47,000
One of those

465
00:24:47,100 --> 00:24:51,266
"Toilet adventures", as I come back from them,

466
00:24:52,066 --> 00:24:57,200
I believe it was about a 01:45 pm.

467
00:25:00,466 --> 00:25:04,366
I go back with my husband and my son to the safe room.

468
00:25:04,366 --> 00:25:06,366
I'm about to enter the safe room,

469
00:25:06,366 --> 00:25:09,000
and I hear someone playing with my door handle,

470
00:25:09,566 --> 00:25:12,033
and in the window next to the door,

471
00:25:12,033 --> 00:25:14,400
I see the barrel of an M16,

472
00:25:15,600 --> 00:25:18,266
and of course the first thing

473
00:25:18,266 --> 00:25:19,833
I think of is to run away

474
00:25:20,966 --> 00:25:23,133
and close the door of the safe room and lock it.

475
00:25:23,866 --> 00:25:26,933
So there were,

476
00:25:28,033 --> 00:25:29,666
there was a person there,

477
00:25:29,800 --> 00:25:31,600
and he could see me in an angle,

478
00:25:31,600 --> 00:25:33,700
but he could see me if he went

479
00:25:33,700 --> 00:25:36,266
he couldn’t shoot me because the angle was too sharp,

480
00:25:36,266 --> 00:25:39,566
through the window like that, through the glass,

481
00:25:39,800 --> 00:25:43,200
and he sees me and he starts shouting:

482
00:25:43,200 --> 00:25:44,966
"IDF, IDF open up!"

483
00:25:45,400 --> 00:25:49,300
So I look at him and I do see that he has IDF uniform,

484
00:25:49,366 --> 00:25:51,633
but you can put on whatever shirt you want,

485
00:25:51,633 --> 00:25:53,400
and it’s my children over here,

486
00:25:53,866 --> 00:25:56,300
and I don’t know what to do,

487
00:25:56,366 --> 00:25:59,100
and I turn around again to go to the safe room.

488
00:25:59,200 --> 00:26:01,400
I'm right next to the door of the safe room,

489
00:26:02,166 --> 00:26:04,866
and then he starts shouting at me:

490
00:26:04,866 --> 00:26:05,633
"No please",

491
00:26:05,633 --> 00:26:07,500
"Please don’t go, we’re Jewish",

492
00:26:07,500 --> 00:26:08,933
"we swear we’re Jewish"

493
00:26:09,266 --> 00:26:12,866
and then I hear that there's a bunch of men outside

494
00:26:12,866 --> 00:26:17,700
my door and they start shouting Jewish symbols,

495
00:26:17,800 --> 00:26:20,700
so I know that they are from ours.

496
00:26:21,066 --> 00:26:24,400
They said "today is Simchat Torah",

497
00:26:24,400 --> 00:26:26,766
"we were supposed to do Hakafot in the evening",

498
00:26:27,166 --> 00:26:29,200
"we’re just in the middle of Hagei Tishrei",

499
00:26:29,200 --> 00:26:30,933
"we just finished Yom Kippur"

500
00:26:33,966 --> 00:26:36,166
And I try to think as fast as I can,

501
00:26:36,833 --> 00:26:38,066
should I trust it, should I not,

502
00:26:38,066 --> 00:26:39,500
what should I do?

503
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:41,433
And then I get this idea,

504
00:26:41,433 --> 00:26:42,966
and apparently I wasn't the only one,

505
00:26:42,966 --> 00:26:45,400
there were plenty of people who thought of that,

506
00:26:45,766 --> 00:26:48,100
I asked them to pray. I say,

507
00:26:48,100 --> 00:26:50,666
"If you’re Jewish I want to hear a Jewish prayer"

508
00:26:52,033 --> 00:26:53,833
Because I thought it would be something

509
00:26:53,833 --> 00:26:55,866
that is very difficult to mimic,

510
00:26:55,866 --> 00:26:57,533
a prayer.

511
00:26:59,033 --> 00:27:01,366
And they started praying.

512
00:27:02,666 --> 00:27:05,000
And I open the door and until today,

513
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:06,933
my husband laughs at me that

514
00:27:06,966 --> 00:27:09,533
my husband at my wedding did not get such a hug,

515
00:27:09,766 --> 00:27:11,900
I fell on this guy's neck

516
00:27:11,900 --> 00:27:15,700
and the first thing that we thought was "Yay".

517
00:27:15,700 --> 00:27:18,866
"The IDF is here it’s over"

518
00:27:19,866 --> 00:27:24,766
But we were so far from the truth.

519
00:27:25,400 --> 00:27:28,833
It wasn't the IDF as an army.

520
00:27:28,833 --> 00:27:33,833
The IDF as an army lost that day.

521
00:27:33,833 --> 00:27:36,866
It’s very difficult to comprehend it,

522
00:27:37,033 --> 00:27:37,700
trust me,

523
00:27:37,700 --> 00:27:42,600
for Israelis it’s even way harder to comprehend it,

524
00:27:42,666 --> 00:27:45,266
but the IDF lost the battle that day.

525
00:27:45,800 --> 00:27:48,900
The people who came were actually private people

526
00:27:48,900 --> 00:27:50,233
from around the country,

527
00:27:50,233 --> 00:27:51,466
who saw the news,

528
00:27:51,666 --> 00:27:55,766
and call their friends and came in

529
00:27:55,766 --> 00:27:57,833
and put on their uniform and their weapons,

530
00:27:57,833 --> 00:27:59,266
in huge groups.

531
00:27:59,266 --> 00:28:01,066
They were friends from the army,

532
00:28:01,300 --> 00:28:04,866
and they just came down in huge groups,

533
00:28:07,233 --> 00:28:08,600
to help.

534
00:28:14,400 --> 00:28:17,900
From that moment on,

535
00:28:17,900 --> 00:28:23,366
we stayed 12 more hours in the safe room with horrible,

536
00:28:23,366 --> 00:28:26,533
horrible battles going on all around us.

537
00:28:26,800 --> 00:28:29,166
The things that this girl,

538
00:28:29,166 --> 00:28:33,500
that fourten-and-half-year-old was telling me by WhatsApp,

539
00:28:33,500 --> 00:28:37,666
in the morning arrived to my neighborhood,

540
00:28:38,400 --> 00:28:40,033
and I can feel,

541
00:28:40,033 --> 00:28:44,133
it already started at 10:30 when the first,

542
00:28:44,266 --> 00:28:48,600
when the second wave of terrorist came

543
00:28:49,633 --> 00:28:51,133
into my neighborhood.

544
00:28:51,666 --> 00:28:54,100
There were plenty of stories in my neighborhood,

545
00:28:54,100 --> 00:28:55,466
there was

546
00:28:56,066 --> 00:29:00,666
an 80 year old man that said to his family

547
00:29:00,666 --> 00:29:04,800
to go to the safe room while he sat in the living room,

548
00:29:04,800 --> 00:29:09,000
Right in front of the big window to be seen first.

549
00:29:09,266 --> 00:29:12,466
His thought was, his plan was, that they will see him,

550
00:29:12,466 --> 00:29:15,800
shoot him and continue, and his family will be saved.

551
00:29:15,800 --> 00:29:17,600
And that's exactly what happened,

552
00:29:18,833 --> 00:29:21,033
they shot him dead,

553
00:29:21,033 --> 00:29:22,566
he was sitting in the living room,

554
00:29:22,566 --> 00:29:24,100
just in front of the window,

555
00:29:24,566 --> 00:29:28,833
acting as if he was reading the newspaper

556
00:29:28,833 --> 00:29:30,966
he was shot dead but they continued going,

557
00:29:30,966 --> 00:29:33,800
and they didn’t go after his family.

558
00:29:41,466 --> 00:29:42,266
Really...

559
00:29:44,600 --> 00:29:47,266
We hear, I can’t even...

560
00:29:48,866 --> 00:29:52,066
All you hear all day long are the explosions,

561
00:29:52,433 --> 00:29:56,300
and if there's something that I really,

562
00:29:56,933 --> 00:30:00,366
really hope that you will never hear in your life,

563
00:30:00,433 --> 00:30:04,700
is a rocket falling just 2 meters,

564
00:30:04,700 --> 00:30:05,800
3 meters from you.

565
00:30:05,800 --> 00:30:10,000
This is something that shakes your entire soul and body,

566
00:30:10,000 --> 00:30:13,366
and this was the noise that

567
00:30:13,366 --> 00:30:16,266
I couldn’t get out of my head for like

568
00:30:16,266 --> 00:30:17,666
a year and a half.

569
00:30:19,800 --> 00:30:21,666
Wow it was so...

570
00:30:23,700 --> 00:30:26,866
They launch the rockets right on the houses.

571
00:30:26,966 --> 00:30:29,500
The house behind mine

572
00:30:29,833 --> 00:30:34,000
was the first one to get hit by a rocket that day,

573
00:30:34,366 --> 00:30:36,700
and we were very worried about the family,

574
00:30:36,700 --> 00:30:38,300
that was there for the entire time,

575
00:30:38,300 --> 00:30:41,566
because they also didn’t have infrastructures,

576
00:30:41,566 --> 00:30:43,133
and they couldn’t communicate.

577
00:30:43,300 --> 00:30:46,866
I ended up calling the mother

578
00:30:46,866 --> 00:30:48,500
of the husband.

579
00:30:49,400 --> 00:30:50,666
She was abroad.

580
00:30:50,666 --> 00:30:51,866
Poor, poor woman.

581
00:30:51,866 --> 00:30:55,066
And I didn’t know that she's also from our kibbutz,

582
00:30:55,800 --> 00:30:57,466
and I didn’t want to panic her,

583
00:30:57,466 --> 00:30:58,433
I said like

584
00:30:58,433 --> 00:30:59,600
"No, everything is under control",

585
00:30:59,600 --> 00:31:02,466
I didn’t tell her that I was worried about them.

586
00:31:02,566 --> 00:31:03,966
End of the day they were okay,

587
00:31:03,966 --> 00:31:05,933
we sent the army over there to check.

588
00:31:10,366 --> 00:31:12,400
The other noise that was very,

589
00:31:12,400 --> 00:31:16,266
very significant that day was of the weapons

590
00:31:16,266 --> 00:31:17,166
Like...

591
00:31:18,033 --> 00:31:19,900
You hear it,

592
00:31:19,900 --> 00:31:22,933
we heard it 20 hours non stop,

593
00:31:23,433 --> 00:31:25,266
and that was

594
00:31:25,266 --> 00:31:26,900
a sound that was very difficult for me

595
00:31:26,900 --> 00:31:28,200
to get out of my head.

596
00:31:28,266 --> 00:31:30,733
After we were evacuated from the kibbutz,

597
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:33,133
I think it was a month after,

598
00:31:33,266 --> 00:31:36,766
I was sitting with friends outside in the evening,

599
00:31:37,066 --> 00:31:39,466
and suddenly I hear that noise, that...

600
00:31:40,400 --> 00:31:43,233
And I just get up and I duck,

601
00:31:44,766 --> 00:31:46,066
And I look around me,

602
00:31:46,066 --> 00:31:49,666
and I see a woman walking with a stroller on pebbles,

603
00:31:50,033 --> 00:31:51,766
and I hear a battlefield.

604
00:31:52,400 --> 00:31:57,533
So that was really made me understand

605
00:31:59,233 --> 00:32:01,000
that it’s going to take a while,

606
00:32:01,566 --> 00:32:02,866
until that trauma...

607
00:32:03,200 --> 00:32:06,066
We were like zombies for quite a long time.

608
00:32:07,000 --> 00:32:11,800
One thing I remember very vividly

609
00:32:11,800 --> 00:32:16,533
is that

610
00:32:17,566 --> 00:32:19,766
when they said that they are going to evacuate us,

611
00:32:19,766 --> 00:32:23,266
it was around 9:00 pm,

612
00:32:24,600 --> 00:32:25,733
and we got a message

613
00:32:25,733 --> 00:32:28,766
saying that we are going to get evacuated,

614
00:32:29,100 --> 00:32:32,000
but they said do not get out of the safe rooms.

615
00:32:32,433 --> 00:32:34,366
Only when soldiers come to your house,

616
00:32:34,366 --> 00:32:35,266
and then you will have 2,

617
00:32:35,266 --> 00:32:37,400
3 minutes to gather things that you need,

618
00:32:37,500 --> 00:32:38,800
and you will go out.

619
00:32:40,033 --> 00:32:43,166
And, it was already 2:00 am,

620
00:32:49,300 --> 00:32:54,066
It was already 2:00 am and they still haven’t reached

621
00:32:54,666 --> 00:32:57,800
my neighborhood. Almost 2:00.

622
00:32:58,700 --> 00:33:01,100
and...

623
00:33:01,100 --> 00:33:03,300
the WhatsApp groups of the women

624
00:33:03,300 --> 00:33:05,266
were very active that day.

625
00:33:05,700 --> 00:33:08,133
So my neighbors and I,

626
00:33:09,066 --> 00:33:12,400
we had the "2:00 am pact", we call it,

627
00:33:12,966 --> 00:33:13,766
we said,

628
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:16,866
we spoke on the phone, we said, okay,

629
00:33:16,866 --> 00:33:19,500
the people that are evacuating us,

630
00:33:19,500 --> 00:33:20,566
they don’t know the kibbutz,

631
00:33:20,566 --> 00:33:22,500
they don’t know who's in every house,

632
00:33:22,566 --> 00:33:26,066
and we need to make sure that nobody is forgotten.

633
00:33:26,600 --> 00:33:30,066
So we had a list of all the names of

634
00:33:30,300 --> 00:33:32,100
my closest

635
00:33:32,100 --> 00:33:34,066
neighbors.

636
00:33:34,066 --> 00:33:35,300
We said, if they get here,

637
00:33:35,300 --> 00:33:38,366
we vowed that if the army gets here,

638
00:33:38,366 --> 00:33:40,600
we make sure that they take everyone.

639
00:33:40,600 --> 00:33:42,866
I had a list: Katia, Ravid,

640
00:33:42,866 --> 00:33:44,100
Adi, Yochi...

641
00:33:44,100 --> 00:33:45,166
I had a list,

642
00:33:45,166 --> 00:33:48,200
I had to make sure that they are being evacuated

643
00:33:48,200 --> 00:33:52,133
when I was evacuated, and we all had that agreement.

644
00:33:59,400 --> 00:34:01,500
One thing that you have to understand is that

645
00:34:01,500 --> 00:34:05,500
we didn’t have a clue about what was going on.

646
00:34:05,500 --> 00:34:07,366
I didn’t know about the Nova (Festival),

647
00:34:07,366 --> 00:34:09,400
I didn’t know about, I had no idea,

648
00:34:09,400 --> 00:34:11,266
I was in my safe room,

649
00:34:11,400 --> 00:34:14,266
and apart from getting text messages,

650
00:34:14,366 --> 00:34:16,333
I didn’t know.

651
00:34:18,233 --> 00:34:20,600
They took us to...

652
00:34:21,033 --> 00:34:25,066
They found this place in the kibbutz,

653
00:34:25,066 --> 00:34:28,766
in one of the places in the outskirts of the kibbutz.

654
00:34:28,766 --> 00:34:29,966
Far from the...

655
00:34:31,100 --> 00:34:33,066
Far, farther away from Gaza,

656
00:34:33,400 --> 00:34:34,733
and they brought...

657
00:34:35,100 --> 00:34:39,400
They always brought about 50 people to that place,

658
00:34:39,400 --> 00:34:42,266
they brought a bus and

659
00:34:42,266 --> 00:34:43,900
sent them away from the kibbutz.

660
00:34:44,633 --> 00:34:47,466
So because it took it took so long,

661
00:34:48,400 --> 00:34:50,900
they started from

662
00:34:50,900 --> 00:34:54,066
the neighborhoods that were attacked

663
00:34:54,066 --> 00:34:57,066
a lot harsher than mine,

664
00:34:59,600 --> 00:35:00,700
it took us time.

665
00:35:01,400 --> 00:35:04,733
So they put us on a bus,

666
00:35:06,200 --> 00:35:09,033
they took us to a place called Mishmar HaNegev,

667
00:35:09,033 --> 00:35:12,200
which is about 40 minutes drive.

668
00:35:12,766 --> 00:35:15,166
The kibbutz was filled with bodies,

669
00:35:16,800 --> 00:35:22,866
and I thanked god for not taking me at 9:00 pm,

670
00:35:23,266 --> 00:35:28,100
but taking me at 2:00 am, so my children couldn’t see,

671
00:35:28,200 --> 00:35:33,066
it was so dark outside, so it was spared from them,

672
00:35:33,066 --> 00:35:35,866
that ended up to be a blessing.

673
00:35:39,600 --> 00:35:42,533
Horrible, horrible views.

674
00:35:45,800 --> 00:35:47,100
On the roads...

675
00:35:49,166 --> 00:35:50,500
Horrible views.

676
00:35:51,100 --> 00:35:53,200
I speak with a friend from Mefalsim,

677
00:35:56,366 --> 00:36:02,100
She gets out of her kibbutz to evacuate because

678
00:36:02,100 --> 00:36:05,100
they weren't evacuated because

679
00:36:05,500 --> 00:36:07,400
they were not the closest to the border,

680
00:36:07,400 --> 00:36:10,100
and they managed

681
00:36:10,266 --> 00:36:11,533
to defeat,

682
00:36:12,300 --> 00:36:14,033
they had much less,

683
00:36:14,666 --> 00:36:17,766
less terrorists came and they were able to defeat them.

684
00:36:20,100 --> 00:36:21,200
So people said "okay,"

685
00:36:21,200 --> 00:36:22,300
"Mefalsim,"

686
00:36:22,300 --> 00:36:24,266
"They got it going everything is fine".

687
00:36:24,433 --> 00:36:30,700
And then she drives out of her kibbutz and she's saying,

688
00:36:31,400 --> 00:36:32,800
she's saying to me:

689
00:36:35,400 --> 00:36:38,600
"Everybody is... It’s like a graveyard",

690
00:36:39,866 --> 00:36:41,900
And, she gets crazy she's going like

691
00:36:41,900 --> 00:36:44,166
"Everybody's dead, everybody's dead",

692
00:36:44,233 --> 00:36:47,366
She starts screaming,

693
00:36:47,366 --> 00:36:49,466
she calls her husband,

694
00:36:49,966 --> 00:36:51,366
and he just

695
00:36:51,366 --> 00:36:53,366
guides her on,

696
00:36:53,433 --> 00:36:55,333
he says "Step on the gas",

697
00:36:55,400 --> 00:36:57,233
"Step on the gas, keep on going".

698
00:36:57,233 --> 00:36:59,000
"Keep on going, you can do this",

699
00:36:59,266 --> 00:37:01,500
And she,

700
00:37:02,033 --> 00:37:03,966
her alone with her children,

701
00:37:05,600 --> 00:37:07,900
It was a horror.

702
00:37:07,900 --> 00:37:11,366
It was a scene from a horror...

703
00:37:13,000 --> 00:37:14,466
Not even a movie,

704
00:37:14,466 --> 00:37:16,566
it’s completely reality,

705
00:37:17,100 --> 00:37:19,166
and they...

706
00:37:22,833 --> 00:37:25,100
We were evacuated to Mishmar HaNegev,

707
00:37:25,300 --> 00:37:26,700
and I will always,

708
00:37:26,700 --> 00:37:31,900
in my life, remember, that in Mishmar HaNegev,

709
00:37:31,900 --> 00:37:33,866
they put some

710
00:37:33,866 --> 00:37:36,466
tea and coffee and some cakes for us,

711
00:37:36,700 --> 00:37:38,466
and in order to get to the hall,

712
00:37:38,466 --> 00:37:40,066
where everybody was gathering,

713
00:37:40,066 --> 00:37:44,633
I needed to take few steps and step down,

714
00:37:44,633 --> 00:37:46,300
go down to the place,

715
00:37:47,000 --> 00:37:49,000
I call it "The stairs of death".

716
00:37:50,300 --> 00:37:55,866
Every step I took I heard of another friend

717
00:37:58,566 --> 00:38:00,400
that I will never see again.

718
00:38:03,966 --> 00:38:06,866
It was the start of a body count

719
00:38:09,066 --> 00:38:10,800
that we had to

720
00:38:13,800 --> 00:38:15,700
to face and

721
00:38:15,700 --> 00:38:18,500
It was a very long one because

722
00:38:19,000 --> 00:38:20,833
firstly,

723
00:38:20,833 --> 00:38:22,500
there were people that we didn’t know

724
00:38:22,500 --> 00:38:25,000
whether they were kidnapped,

725
00:38:25,000 --> 00:38:28,466
or murdered brutally and we cannot identify the body,

726
00:38:29,633 --> 00:38:34,033
there were people from other kibbutzim that...

727
00:38:34,033 --> 00:38:35,800
There was this thing.

728
00:38:36,666 --> 00:38:38,066
Between everyone.

729
00:38:38,633 --> 00:38:42,966
We were scared of sending messages to friends

730
00:38:43,500 --> 00:38:46,033
from other kibbutzim. It took us

731
00:38:46,033 --> 00:38:47,066
3, 4 days.

732
00:38:47,633 --> 00:38:49,700
We were looking for lists,

733
00:38:51,266 --> 00:38:54,866
And, when we finally did send messages,

734
00:38:54,866 --> 00:38:59,033
it was more or less the same all around the region.

735
00:38:59,033 --> 00:39:01,800
It was "just give us a sign of life"

736
00:39:09,766 --> 00:39:10,566
Oh...

737
00:39:13,500 --> 00:39:15,066
Every message like that,

738
00:39:15,066 --> 00:39:17,033
that I got from a friend, was like

739
00:39:17,033 --> 00:39:17,566
"Oh my God"...

740
00:39:17,566 --> 00:39:20,033
"She's alive" or "he's alive".

741
00:39:20,033 --> 00:39:21,766
"Oh my God thank God"

742
00:39:26,200 --> 00:39:29,000
And every answer that I got,

743
00:39:29,566 --> 00:39:30,233
there were people,

744
00:39:30,233 --> 00:39:33,666
I didn’t have the guts to send a message to.

745
00:39:33,900 --> 00:39:36,466
I just waited for them to contact me.

746
00:39:43,400 --> 00:39:46,033
So, every day and for a long time,

747
00:39:46,400 --> 00:39:50,933
you hear, you’re going from a funeral to a memorial to a...

748
00:39:53,033 --> 00:39:55,000
To give your condolences,

749
00:39:55,000 --> 00:39:56,400
it’s just, we just couldn’t.

750
00:39:57,966 --> 00:40:00,666
The amounts were horrific.

751
00:40:07,600 --> 00:40:09,466
And, then it took us a very long time,

752
00:40:09,466 --> 00:40:10,966
to get back on our feet,

753
00:40:10,966 --> 00:40:13,666
I can’t even say that we’re back on our feet yet,

754
00:40:14,400 --> 00:40:19,033
I can say that very good people from Israel,

755
00:40:19,033 --> 00:40:20,700
and from around the world,

756
00:40:22,800 --> 00:40:25,200
really many,

757
00:40:25,200 --> 00:40:27,000
especially Jews,

758
00:40:27,000 --> 00:40:30,600
but not only, not only. Many people, Christians.

759
00:40:30,600 --> 00:40:31,733
Oh my God...

760
00:40:31,766 --> 00:40:34,033
We got so much help

761
00:40:34,033 --> 00:40:37,566
from Christians around the world.

762
00:40:39,266 --> 00:40:40,866
We were just

763
00:40:42,800 --> 00:40:46,133
embraced with a very warm embrace.

764
00:40:49,833 --> 00:40:53,566
You asked me earlier about

765
00:40:54,300 --> 00:40:57,666
the Israeli Muslims or Israeli Arabs.

766
00:40:58,033 --> 00:41:00,600
What happened then was that

767
00:41:00,600 --> 00:41:05,066
many of them came also to where we were evacuated to,

768
00:41:05,233 --> 00:41:07,800
And they came also to bring help.

769
00:41:08,166 --> 00:41:11,666
And when I said to one of them,

770
00:41:11,666 --> 00:41:14,100
there was one of them that came with a car,

771
00:41:14,266 --> 00:41:16,366
with a pickup truck,

772
00:41:16,366 --> 00:41:19,566
really filled with aid for us,

773
00:41:20,500 --> 00:41:23,733
and I remember that I said "Thank you",

774
00:41:24,300 --> 00:41:26,333
and he started crying,

775
00:41:27,200 --> 00:41:29,666
and he said to me "Don’t thank me",

776
00:41:29,766 --> 00:41:31,700
"It happened to all of us".

777
00:41:32,233 --> 00:41:35,100
"What happened to you, it happened to all of us"

778
00:41:36,033 --> 00:41:39,066
He said "Every peaceful person of the Middle East,".

779
00:41:39,300 --> 00:41:41,733
"every moderate person of the Middle East,"

780
00:41:44,500 --> 00:41:47,000
"It was an attack of all on all of us",

781
00:41:47,000 --> 00:41:48,900
"so don’t you say thank you."

